1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,500
Before humans mastered fire,

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:05,220
one Titan dared to defy Zeus.

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:09,020
Prometheus saw people shivering in darkness and

4
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:11,420
decided they deserved more than the gods

5
00:00:11,420 --> 00:00:12,000
allowed.

6
00:00:12,800 --> 00:00:14,820
He stole a spark from the divine

7
00:00:14,820 --> 00:00:17,560
realm, hiding it in a hollow fennel

8
00:00:17,560 --> 00:00:20,400
stalk. As the flame passed from hand

9
00:00:20,400 --> 00:00:22,920
to hand, night changed forever.

10
00:00:23,688 --> 00:00:25,300
Fire cooked food,

11
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:28,520
warmed shelters, and made metalwork possible.

12
00:00:29,120 --> 00:00:29,800
In the myth,

13
00:00:30,160 --> 00:00:32,880
a single stolen gift shifted the balance

14
00:00:32,880 --> 00:00:35,131
between immortals and mortals.

15
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,180
Zeus answered not with gratitude,

16
00:00:38,540 --> 00:00:42,260
but punishment. He ordered Prometheus chained to

17
00:00:42,260 --> 00:00:43,220
a remote rock,

18
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:45,660
where a great eagle would tear at

19
00:00:45,660 --> 00:00:46,220
his liver.

20
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,340
The wound renewed,

21
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:50,140
and the torment returned.

22
00:00:50,140 --> 00:00:52,860
Each day the bird descended again.

23
00:00:53,420 --> 00:00:55,420
Yet the Titan remained the figure who

24
00:00:55,420 --> 00:00:57,660
had chosen suffering over obedience.

25
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,200
His story leaves a question burning:

26
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:04,000
when power withholds something essential,

27
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:05,800
is taking it theft,

28
00:01:05,800 --> 00:01:09,680
or liberation? The flame still shines between

29
00:01:09,680 --> 00:01:10,109
them.
